# LTI deliverable Markdown (required content)

## Purpose

Make the **graded consolidated design document** (**`LTI-<CONTRIBUTOR-SLUG>/LTI-<CONTRIBUTOR-SLUG>.md`**) complete, renderable, and auditable against the course checklist. **`prompts.md`** in the same folder is governed by **`.cursor/rules/30-prompt-tracking.mdc`** (logging and deliverable quality)—this rule MUST NOT be treated as applying to **`prompts.md`**, PRDs, **`ADR.md`**, or other **`LTI-*`** Markdown.

## Scope

- **Glob attachment:** files matching **`LTI-<CONTRIBUTOR-SLUG>/LTI-<CONTRIBUTOR-SLUG>.md`** only (same pattern as **`**/LTI-*/LTI-*.md`**; basename aligns with folder per **`.cursor/rules/40-naming-and-paths.mdc`**).
- **Out of scope for this rule:** **`prompts.md`**, **`LTI-<CONTRIBUTOR-SLUG>/<NNN>-prd.md`**, **`ADR.md`**, and any other Markdown under **`LTI-*`** (those files use other rules or templates).

## Requirements — main design document

The file **`LTI-<CONTRIBUTOR-SLUG>/LTI-<CONTRIBUTOR-SLUG>.md`** MUST contain all of the following:

1. **Brief description** of the LTI ATS design, **added value**, and **competitive advantages**.
2. **Main functions** explained clearly (scope and user-facing capabilities).
3. **Lean Canvas** (business model): embedded **Mermaid** or equivalent, or a clear link plus instructions to read it; MUST be legible when rendered (e.g. GitHub).
4. **Three main use cases:** narrative for **each** use case AND **one diagram per use case** (Mermaid or approved equivalent).
5. **Data model:** entities, attributes with **name and type**, and **relationships** (typed, reviewable model—not prose-only placeholders).
6. **High-level system design:** prose **and** a diagram (Mermaid or approved equivalent).
7. **C4-style depth:** **one** component MUST be drilled into **in depth** (diagram + explanation), consistent with **`.cursor/rules/50-diagram-standards.mdc`**.

Assistants MUST use **Mermaid** where the course expects diagrams unless the user explicitly chooses another repo-friendly format that still renders in the target viewer.

## Prohibited behavior

- MUST NOT omit the main deliverable file or **`prompts.md`** for a complete course submission.
- MUST NOT substitute a single wall of text for **required diagrams** where the checklist calls for a diagram per item.
- MUST NOT use **vague attribute lists** without **types** where the checklist requires **name and type**.

## Verification (before calling a deliverable “complete”)

- [ ] All seven main-document bullets above are present and labeled clearly enough for a grader to find.
- [ ] Three use cases each have **both** narrative **and** a diagram.
- [ ] Data model lists **types**, not only entity names.
- [ ] Diagrams render as fenced code blocks or valid image links; no broken Mermaid fence markers.

## Language

Course materials may be EN/ES; the **deliverable language** MUST stay **consistent within one** `LTI-*` folder unless the user explicitly switches.
